content.file_manager_thunar:
System file management is provided by Thunar, known for its fast directory indexing and clean GTK 3 interface. Key features include:

- Tabbed navigation and dual-pane split view browsing;
- Built-in bulk file renamer utility (`thunar-bulk-rename`) supporting regular expression search-and-replace and date formatting;
- Custom user actions enabling arbitrary shell command integration in context menus;
- Seamless remote volume mounting (Samba, SFTP, WebDAV) managed by the GVFS daemon.

content.hardware_support_and_architectures:
Xubuntu targets the 64-bit `x86_64` (amd64) architecture, having dropped 32-bit (i386) installation media in 2019 (Xubuntu 19.04). System requirements remain modest:

- Processor: 64-bit dual-core CPU (1.5 GHz or higher);
- Memory (RAM): Minimum 1.5 GB RAM; 2 GB recommended for general office tasks; 4 GB recommended for modern web browsing;
- Storage: 10 GB for Xubuntu Minimal; 20 GB recommended for Xubuntu Desktop;
- Firmware: Full support for legacy BIOS and UEFI firmware, with out-of-the-box Secure Boot via Canonical's signed `shim` loader.
